        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 1.59,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] Now actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.59,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "before I'll output the annual data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "in a table on the screen, I'll do something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "I'll outsource this type definition here into a model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "which is not something you have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "but something that can make your code a bit leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "and easier to reuse.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 23.943,
          "en": "For that, I'll add a new file here in my app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.08,
          "end": 30.08,
          "en": "and I'll name it investment-input.model.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.27,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "The file name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "but of course it should describe what's inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 36.45,
          "en": "and it should follow this convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 38.28,
          "en": "of having this description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.28,
          "end": 42.06,
          "en": "of which kind of thing you'll store in that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "if it's a component, a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 46.443,
          "en": "or in this case a data model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "Now model is a big word here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "In the end in there, I want to create a custom object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "with help of this interface keyword provided by TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 61.86,
          "en": "which I'll name investment input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.86,
          "end": 64.563,
          "en": "to be in line with my file name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.15,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "and then I'll paste in that object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 70.773,
          "en": "as we defined it earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "Alternatively, instead of using an interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 79.23,
          "en": "you could have also used the type keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.23,
          "end": 82.743,
          "en": "to create this type, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.91,
          "end": 86.16,
          "en": "It's up to you what you want to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "Here, I'll go for the interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "since that's the approach you'll see a bit more often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 93.243,
          "en": "in Angular projects in my experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 98.19,
          "en": "Now we definitely need to export it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "We also would need to do that with the custom type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 103.71000000000001,
          "en": "to make it available outside of this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.71000000000001,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "because the idea now is to import this custom type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 112.35300000000001,
          "en": "in all the places where such a object type is expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "So in the app component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "I'll now replace this object type definition here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 123.75,
          "en": "by using my investment input type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.75,
          "end": 126.57,
          "en": "And for that we must import it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.57,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "and we can add the type keyword in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "to make it clear that this is just a type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "And we then assign it as a type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 136.713,
          "en": "for this data parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.45,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "And it's now not just here where we can use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 145.41,
          "en": "but also in the user input component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.41,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "there on this event emitter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 152.463,
          "en": "it's now also this investment input type that we can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.63,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "And here we also must make sure that this import was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 161.643,
          "en": "and we can add this type addition here to the import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 168.483,
          "en": "With that, of course, the program will still work as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.04,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "but we made our code a bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 174.6,
          "en": "But now I wanna make sure that the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.6,
          "end": 176.853,
          "en": "is actually also output on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
